<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Napoleon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1769">1769</a>–<a href="/years/1821">1821</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Napoleon Bonaparte</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Napoleon Bonaparte was a French military leader who seized power after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a> and ruled as Emperor of the French. His conquests reshaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>: he dissolved the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1812, and his occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> helped trigger the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. His invasion of Portugal drove the Portuguese court to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> in 1808, a step towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon.jpg" alt="Napoleon" width="252" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacques-Louis David · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jacques-Louis_David_-_The_Emperor_Napoleon_in_His_Study_at_the_Tuileries_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
